From 6696c62185b72c16b7d0e2a2bfd160e5d2b8548a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kernel-rg35xx <build@localhost>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 09:16:15 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] input: gpio_keys_polled: RG35XX Gamepad Driver recovered from
 the installed module

Black-Seraph's out-of-tree "RG35XX Gamepad Driver" (GPL v2, source never published) rebuilt from the
installed gpio_keys_polled.ko: built-in 22 button key map, one bit mask per poll and one sync, board
revision detection (START/SELECT/MENU/L3/R3 on GPIO 14/15/16/20/19 or 85/84/71/72/73: the set reading
pressed is masked), /sys/class/volume/value through the codec's allen_adjust_volume (libmsettings), and
an input handler recording KEY_POWER. Same name, ids and capabilities (SDL GUID and evdev key order).
As a module every function and data object matches the original (layout and register allocation aside).
Built in: late_initcall_sync, so the gamepad stays /dev/input/event1 after atc260x_onoff (evmapy
event1.json configs).
---
 drivers/input/keyboard/gpio_keys_polled.c | 445 +++++++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 311 insertions(+), 134 deletions(-)

